{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532183586,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5252ffeattb2EUQkGXt4x","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2740c53001A9eMXmZCvaNMzC","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5252ffeattb2EUQkGXt4x","messageID":"msg_1d273ed05001lJcEmBvBFScKjW","type":"tool","id":"call_bfd16e043d494a328379a58e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md","limit":80},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: name: sk-doc\n3: description: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\n4: allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n5: version: 2.9.13.0\n6: metadata:\n7:   family: sk-util\n8: ---\n9: \n10: <!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n11: \n12: # Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n13: \n14: One advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n15: `sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\n16: It holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\n17: The cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n18: \n19: **Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n24: \n25: Use this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n26: \n27: | Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n28: |------|------------|--------|---------|\n29: | **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n30: | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder README, general or code-folder | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n31: | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n32: | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n33: | **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n34: | **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n35: | **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n36: | **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n37: | **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n38: | **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n39: | **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n40: | **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n41: | **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n42: | **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n43: \n44: ### When NOT to Use\n45: - Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n46: - Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n47: - Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n48: - A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n49: - The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n54: \n55: Routing is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\n56: Stage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\n57: The `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n58: `sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\n59: Stage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\n60: The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n61: The advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\n62: Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n63: Act on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n64: Compiled routing is the default.\n65: An unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n66: Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n71: \n72: ### Terms\n73: \n74: - **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n75: - **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n76: - **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n77: - **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n78: - **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n79: - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n80: - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: name: sk-doc\n3: description: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\n4: allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n5: version: 2.9.13.0\n6: metadata:\n7:   family: sk-util\n8: ---\n9: \n10: <!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n11: \n12: # Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n13: \n14: One advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n15: `sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\n16: It holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\n17: The cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n18: \n19: **Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n24: \n25: Use this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n26: \n27: | Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n28: |------|------------|--------|---------|\n29: | **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n30: | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder README, general or code-folder | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n31: | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n32: | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n33: | **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n34: | **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n35: | **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n36: | **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n37: | **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n38: | **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n39: | **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n40: | **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n41: | **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n42: | **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n43: \n44: ### When NOT to Use\n45: - Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n46: - Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n47: - Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n48: - A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n49: - The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n54: \n55: Routing is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\n56: Stage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\n57: The `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n58: `sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\n59: Stage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\n60: The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n61: The advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\n62: Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n63: Act on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n64: Compiled routing is the default.\n65: An unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n66: Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n71: \n72: ### Terms\n73: \n74: - **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n75: - **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n76: - **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n77: - **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n78: - **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n79: - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n80: - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\"limit\":80}"},"time":{"start":1794532183123,"end":1794532183586}}}}
