{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532203565,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5252ffeattb2EUQkGXt4x","part":{"partID":"prt_1d274598a002o4HFnDJoo1Ig7T","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5252ffeattb2EUQkGXt4x","messageID":"msg_1d274513e001J77qsFIOJ8mIkI","type":"tool","id":"call_81216d99d99f4df0a1531f7b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\nindex ef9b603323..44c6998a3d 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\n@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n |---|---|\n | `command-scope.cjs` | Authored exceptions for runtime-exclusive commands and runtime-native commands. |\n | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` | Derives expected mirror links, checks drift and writes missing or stale links when invoked without `--check`. Its `dsh-adapters` tree expects one link in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/` per `.mjs` adapter in a `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` folder, aimed at the adapter's real file. |\n-| `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` | Writes the Gate 1 lookup pointer block into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` from the root `AGENTS.md` line. Codex reads the root file as project instructions and needs no block; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n+| `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` | Writes two pointer blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` from the root `AGENTS.md` lines: the Gate 1 lookup, and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct advisor call. Codex reads the root file as project instructions and needs no block; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n | `hook-registry.json` | The canonical hook set: every hook once, with its concern, script and per-runtime event bindings; Pi's entry file name per hook. |\n | `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` | Renders the four JSON hook registration files from the registry in each runtime's shape and verifies the Pi entry files, each a one-line re-export; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\nindex ef9b603323..44c6998a3d 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\n@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n |---|---|\n | `command-scope.cjs` | Authored exceptions for runtime-exclusive commands and runtime-native commands. |\n | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` | Derives expected mirror links, checks drift and writes missing or stale links when invoked without `--check`. Its `dsh-adapters` tree expects one link in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/` per `.mjs` adapter in a `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` folder, aimed at the adapter's real file. |\n-| `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` | Writes the Gate 1 lookup pointer block into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` from the root `AGENTS.md` line. Codex reads the root file as project instructions and needs no block; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n+| `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` | Writes two pointer blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` from the root `AGENTS.md` lines: the Gate 1 lookup, and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct advisor call. Codex reads the root file as project instructions and needs no block; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n | `hook-registry.json` | The canonical hook set: every hook once, with its concern, script and per-runtime event bindings; Pi's entry file name per hook. |\n | `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` | Renders the four JSON hook registration files from the registry in each runtime's shape and verifies the Pi entry files, each a one-line re-export; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n \n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532202890,"end":1794532203565}}}}
