{"type":"text","timestamp":1794532219124,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5252ffeattb2EUQkGXt4x","part":{"id":"prt_1d27490e9001Vf9iccjLoUbQhE","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e5252ffeattb2EUQkGXt4x","messageID":"msg_1d2748a04001YDSWynnx7k7k3j","type":"text","text":"T021 is complete. One row of the runtime-mirrors README now says the script writes both pointer blocks.\n\n**File written**\n`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` line 26, the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row. It now says the script writes two pointer blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup, and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct advisor call. The rest of the row and the rest of the file are unchanged, confirmed by the scoped diff.\n\n**Verify output**\n```\n26:| `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` | Writes two pointer blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` from the root `AGENTS.md` lines: the Gate 1 lookup, and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct advisor call. Codex reads the root file as project instructions and needs no block; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\nexit=0\n```\n\n**Not done**\nI did not tick the T021 checkbox, as instructed. Nothing was blocked. I touched no other file and ran no git write command.\n\nThe operator's next step is the remaining Wave 2 tasks, then T024 to regenerate the manifest and T025 to regenerate the Cursor rule.","time":{"start":1794532217065,"end":1794532219124}}}
